# Permanent GitHub Distribution Compliance

This rule is permanent and supersedes any older documentation or distribution instruction.

## Prohibited Patterns in README.md and Repository Documentation

Never include in `README.md`, `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, or any other committed repository documentation, generated page, or badge:

- Direct executable download links (`.exe`, `.apk`, `.msi`, `.dmg`).
- Direct archive download links (`.zip`, `.tar.gz`).
- Direct checksum download links (`SHA256SUMS.txt`).
- Download buttons or download badges linking directly to executable or archive assets.
- Any `/releases/download/` or `/releases/latest/download/` URL.
- Any `browser_download_url` link.
- Redirect services, URL shorteners, external download mirrors, download proxy services, or disguised/indirect artifact download mechanisms.

## Approved Distribution Pattern

- All compiled executables, portable packages, source archives, release notes, and SHA-256 checksums must remain exclusively in the repository's native GitHub Releases section (`https://github.com/ShamelesAbyss/Hydra/releases`).
- `README.md` may include an ordinary informational link to the repository's native GitHub Releases page using neutral wording:
  "Compiled executables, portable packages, source archives, release notes and SHA-256 checksums are available through the repository's GitHub Releases section."
- Informational badges (version, CI workflow status, offline tests, language, license, audit, platform support) are permitted only when they do not link directly to downloadable binary/archive/checksum assets.
- All artwork, banners, diagrams, and screenshots in `README.md` must use locally committed repository files under `docs/assets/` with exact case-sensitive relative paths.

## Automated Enforcement

Run `./.github/scripts/verify-github-compliance.ps1` locally and in GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/verify.yml` and `.github/workflows/release.yml`) before every commit and release. Do not remove or weaken this rule without explicit owner authorization and clarification from GitHub Support.
